1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:14,000
It’s 7pm on a balmy Saturday night in June, and I have just ordered my first beer in I Cervejaria, a restaurant in Zambujeira do Mar, one of the prettiest villages on Portugal’s south-west coast.
现在是六月一个和暖的周六晚上7点，我刚在I Cervejaria餐馆点了第一杯啤酒，这家餐馆位于赞布热拉杜马尔，那是葡萄牙西南海岸最漂亮的村庄之一。

2
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:18,190
The place is empty, but this doesn’t surprise me at all.
店里空荡荡的，不过我一点也不意外。

3
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:28,160
I have spent two weeks in this area, driving along empty roads, playing with my son on empty beaches, and staying in B&Bs where we are the only guests.
我已经在这一带待了两个星期，开车行驶在空荡荡的公路上，和儿子在空无一人的海滩上玩耍，住的民宿里也只有我们这一拨客人。

4
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:39,190
No doubt the restaurant, run by two brothers for the past 28 years, is buzzing in July and August, when Portuguese holidaymakers descend on the Alentejo coast.
七、八月间，葡萄牙的度假者纷纷涌向阿连特茹海岸，那时这家由两兄弟经营了28年的餐馆想必热闹非凡。

5
00:00:39,990 --> 00:00:52,040
But for the other 10 months of the year, the trickle of diners who come to feast on fantastically fresh seafood reflects the general pace of life in the Alentejo: sleepy, bordering on comatose.
但在一年中其余的10个月里，只有零零星星的食客来这里大啖新鲜至极的海鲜，这反映出阿连特茹总体的生活节奏：昏昏欲睡，近乎昏迷。

6
00:00:52,840 --> 00:01:02,450
One of the poorest, least-developed, least-populated regions in western Europe, the Alentejo has been dubbed both the Provence and the Tuscany of Portugal.
阿连特茹是西欧最贫穷、最不发达、人口最稀少的地区之一，它既被称作“葡萄牙的普罗旺斯”，也被称作“葡萄牙的托斯卡纳”。

7
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:04,540
Neither is accurate.
这两种说法都不准确。

8
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:11,720
Its scenery is not as pretty and, apart from in the capital Evora, its food isn’t as sophisticated.
这里的风景不如那两处秀美；除了首府埃武拉，这里的饮食也不如那两处讲究。

9
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:22,540
The charms of this land of wheatfields, cork oak forests, wildflower meadows and tiny white-washed villages are more subtle than in France’s or Italy’s poster regions.
这片土地上有麦田、栓皮栎林、开满野花的草甸，还有一座座刷成白色的小村庄；与法国或意大利那些招牌地区相比，这里的魅力更为含蓄。

10
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:26,990
To travel here is to step back in time 40 or 50 years.
到这里旅行，就如同让时光倒流四五十年。

11
00:01:27,790 --> 00:01:32,570
Life rolls along at a treacly pace; there’s an unnerving stillness to the landscape.
这里的日子过得像糖浆流淌一般缓慢；四下的景致透着一种令人心慌的寂静。

12
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:38,450
But that stillness ends abruptly at the Atlantic Ocean, where there is drama in spades.
但这份寂静到了大西洋边便戛然而止，那里有的是动人心魄的景象。

13
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:52,090
Protected by the South West Alentejo and Costa Vicentina national park, the 100km of coastline from Porto Covo in the Alentejo to Burgau in the Algarve is the most stunning in Europe.
从阿连特茹的波尔图科武到阿尔加维的布尔高，这100公里海岸线受西南阿连特茹与维森蒂娜海岸国家公园保护，是全欧洲最壮美的海岸线。

14
00:01:52,890 --> 00:01:54,960
And yet few people seem to know about it.
可是，似乎很少有人知道这段海岸。

15
00:01:55,760 --> 00:02:05,290
Walkers come to admire the views from the Fisherman’s Way, surfers to ride the best waves in Europe, but day after day we had spectacular beaches to ourselves.
徒步者来这里，在渔夫小径上欣赏风景；冲浪者来这里，驾驭欧洲最好的海浪；可我们日复一日独享着一片片壮观的海滩。

16
00:02:06,090 --> 00:02:17,380
The lack of awareness is partly a matter of accessibility (these beaches are a good two hours’ drive from either Faro or Lisbon airports) and partly to do with a lack of beachside accommodation.
这段海岸鲜为人知，部分是因为交通不便（这些海滩无论离法鲁机场还是里斯本机场，都有足足两个小时的车程），部分则与海滩边缺少住处有关。

17
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:25,830
There are some gorgeous, independent guesthouses in this area (see below), but they are hidden in valleys or at the end of dirt tracks.
这一带有一些独立经营的精美小旅馆（见下文），但都藏在山谷里或土路尽头。

18
00:02:26,630 --> 00:02:39,050
Our base was Herdade da Nespereira, a beautiful 600-acre estate of uncultivated land covered in rock-rose, eucalyptus and wild flowers 13km inland from Zambujeira.
我们的落脚点是内斯佩雷拉庄园，这座美丽的庄园占地600英亩，位于赞布热拉往内陆13公里处，土地未经开垦，长满了岩蔷薇、桉树和野花。

19
00:02:39,850 --> 00:02:46,080
Our one-bedroom home, Azenha, was once home to the miller who tended the now-restored watermill next to it.
我们住的是一套一居室的房子，名叫阿泽尼亚，从前是磨坊主的家；当年他照看的那座水磨坊就在旁边，如今已经修复。

20
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:52,090
A kilometre away from the main house, pool and restaurant, it is gloriously isolated.
小屋离主楼、泳池和餐厅有一公里远，偏僻得妙不可言。

21
00:02:52,890 --> 00:03:00,160
If Julian Assange ever leaves the Ecuadorian embassy in London, I suggest he hotfoots it to an Alentejo hideaway.
要是朱利安·阿桑奇哪天离开了厄瓜多尔驻伦敦大使馆，我建议他火速赶往阿连特茹的某个藏身之所。

22
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,290
He’d be safe for months.
在那里他好几个月都会安然无恙。

23
00:03:03,090 --> 00:03:16,390
Stepping out of the house in the morning to greet our neighbours—wild horses on one side, donkeys on the other—with nothing but birdsong filling the air, I felt a sense of adventure you normally only get with wild camping.
清晨走出屋子，跟邻居们打个招呼——一边是野马，另一边是驴——空中回荡的只有鸟鸣，我体会到一种通常只有野外露营时才有的冒险感。

24
00:03:17,190 --> 00:03:27,040
“When people first arrive, they feel a little anxious wondering what they are going to do the whole time,” Sarah Gredley, the English owner of Nespereira, told me.
“大家刚来的时候，会有点焦虑，不知道待在这儿的这段时间里都要干些什么。”内斯佩雷拉庄园的主人、英国人萨拉·格雷德利对我说。

25
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:34,490
“But it doesn’t usually take them long to realise that the whole point of being here is to slow down, to enjoy nature.”
“不过，他们通常用不了多久就会明白，待在这里的全部意义就在于放慢脚步，享受大自然。”

26
00:03:35,290 --> 00:03:47,130
We followed her advice, walking down to the stream in search of terrapins and otters, or through clusters of cork oak trees, their branches hairy with lichen like the ancient trees of a fairytale forest.
我们听从她的建议，或是往下走到小溪边，寻找水龟和水獭，或是穿过一丛丛栓皮栎，枝条上长满地衣，毛茸茸的，宛如童话森林里的古树。

27
00:03:47,930 --> 00:03:56,290
On some days, we tramped uphill to the windmill, now a romantic house for two, for panoramic views across the estate and beyond.
有几天，我们一路跋涉上坡，走到风车磨坊——如今那里是一座供两人入住的浪漫小屋——去饱览整个庄园乃至更远处的全景。

28
00:03:57,090 --> 00:04:09,370
When we ventured out, we were always drawn back to the coast—the gentle sands and shallow bay of Farol beach close to Vila Nova de Milfontes, the rock pools of Almograve or the cove at Carvalhal.
每次出门探索，我们总会被吸引回海边：新米尔丰特斯附近的法罗尔海滩，沙滩平缓，海湾水浅；阿尔莫格拉维的礁石潮池；或者卡尔瓦利亚尔的小海湾。

29
00:04:10,170 --> 00:04:25,920
At the end of the day, we would head, sandy-footed, to the nearest restaurant, knowing that at every one there would be a cabinet full of fresh seafood to choose from—bass, bream, salmon, lobster, prawns, crabs, goose barnacles, clams … We never ate the same thing twice.
一天下来，我们会带着满脚的沙子去最近的餐馆，心里知道每一家都会有满满一柜新鲜海鲜供人挑选——鲈鱼、鲷鱼、三文鱼、龙虾、大虾、螃蟹、鹅颈藤壶、蛤蜊……我们从来没有吃过重样的菜。

30
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:37,010
A kilometre or so from I Cervejaria, on Zambujeira’s idyllic natural harbour is O Sacas, originally built to feed the fishermen but now popular with everyone.
距离I Cervejaria一公里左右，在赞布热拉田园诗般的天然港湾边，坐落着O Sacas餐馆；它最初是为了给渔民供应饭食而建的，如今却深受大家欢迎。

31
00:04:37,810 --> 00:04:50,300
After scarfing platefuls of seafood on the terrace, we wandered down to the harbour where two fishermen, kitted out in wetsuits, were setting out by boat across the clear turquoise water to collect goose barnacles.
在露台上狼吞虎咽地吃完一盘又一盘海鲜后，我们信步走到港湾边，那里有两个身穿潜水服的渔民正乘船出发，要穿过清澈的碧绿海水去采鹅颈藤壶。

32
00:04:51,100 --> 00:05:02,200
Other than them, the place was deserted—just another empty beauty spot where I wondered for the hundredth time that week how this pristine stretch of coast has remained so undiscovered.
除了他们，那里空无一人——又是一处空荡荡的美景胜地；在这里，那一周里我第一百次纳闷：这段原始纯净的海岸怎么至今仍如此鲜为人知。
